WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.211
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.511 --> 00:00:08.839
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:15.774
Unit nine: Comparative Structures (as...as). Today you will say that two things are equal or not equal.

4
00:00:16.074 --> 00:00:18.854
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.172
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:25.006
As...as.

7
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:28.701
As...as means a pattern that shows equality.

8
00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:30.736
He is as tall as me.

9
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.269
Your turn. Say: As...as.

10
00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.227
As...as.

11
00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:39.787
Equal.

12
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:43.398
Equal means the same in size, number or value.

13
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:45.669
The two prices are equal.

14
00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:48.796
Your turn. Say: Equal.

15
00:00:51.633 --> 00:00:52.495
Equal.

16
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.332
Comparison.

17
00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:58.408
Comparison means looking at how things are alike or different.

18
00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.086
A comparison shows the difference.

19
00:01:01.683 --> 00:01:04.440
Your turn. Say: Comparison.

20
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.324
Comparison.

21
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:10.398
Not as...as.

22
00:01:11.383 --> 00:01:14.718
Not as...as means a pattern that shows something is less.

23
00:01:15.317 --> 00:01:16.794
I am not as tall as him.

24
00:01:17.383 --> 00:01:20.314
Your turn. Say: Not as...as.

25
00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.342
Not as...as.

26
00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:25.864
Same.

27
00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.803
Same means exactly alike.

28
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:30.940
We have the same teacher.

29
00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.237
Your turn. Say: Same.

30
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:37.950
Same.

31
00:01:38.717 --> 00:01:39.625
Different.

32
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:42.233
Different means not the same.

33
00:01:42.817 --> 00:01:44.212
Our bags are different.

34
00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:47.202
Your turn. Say: Different.

35
00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:50.963
Different.

36
00:01:51.717 --> 00:01:52.451
Height.

37
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.018
Height means how tall someone or something is.

38
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:58.291
His height is one metre ninety.

39
00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:01.118
Your turn. Say: Height.

40
00:02:03.967 --> 00:02:04.759
Height.

41
00:02:05.517 --> 00:02:06.355
Speed.

42
00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.535
Speed means how fast something moves.

43
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.836
The speed of the car is high.

44
00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.033
Your turn. Say: Speed.

45
00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:18.763
Speed.

46
00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:23.299
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.661
Visal, you and your friend are both tall. What can you say?

48
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:37.312
I am as tall as my friend. We use as + adjective + as to say two things are equal: She is as clever as her sister.

49
00:02:38.417 --> 00:02:39.929
And if they are not equal?

50
00:02:41.017 --> 00:02:51.926
We use not as + adjective + as: My bag is not as heavy as yours. It means my bag is lighter. We can also say less heavy than yours.

51
00:02:53.017 --> 00:02:54.343
What about the same?

52
00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:07.779
We say the same as: My phone is the same as yours. Notice: same needs the. We say different from: His idea is different from mine. Do not use than after as.

53
00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:10.619
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:15.956
Grammar focus: Equality: as plus adjective plus as and not as … as.

55
00:03:16.256 --> 00:03:17.431
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.117 --> 00:03:19.896
He is as tall as his brother.

57
00:03:20.783 --> 00:03:22.934
My bag is not as heavy as yours.

58
00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.722
My phone is the same as yours.

59
00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:34.195
Use as + adjective + as for equal things and not as + adjective + as for unequal things. Say the same as and different from.

60
00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:38.891
Be careful! Don't say: She is as tall than me.

61
00:03:40.833 --> 00:03:42.705
Say: She is as tall as me.

62
00:03:43.005 --> 00:03:44.366
Use as…as, not than.

63
00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:47.900
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.131
Equal or Not Equal?.

65
00:03:50.431 --> 00:03:53.742
My brother is as tall as me, but he is not as strong.

66
00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:57.139
This book is not as expensive as that one.

67
00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.249
The two cars have the same speed.

68
00:04:01.233 --> 00:04:04.324
Their heights are equal, but their personalities are different.

69
00:04:05.333 --> 00:04:07.275
A comparison helps us choose.

70
00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:12.473
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:14.875
He is as tall blank me.

72
00:04:15.175 --> 00:04:18.225
A, than. B, as. C, like.

73
00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.569
The answer is B: as.

74
00:04:24.717 --> 00:04:27.810
This bag is blank as heavy as that one. (lighter)

75
00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:31.230
A, not. B, no. C, never.

76
00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:36.430
The answer is A: not.

77
00:04:37.583 --> 00:04:39.920
My phone is the same blank yours.

78
00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.805
A, as. B, than. C, to.

79
00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:47.983
The answer is A: as.

80
00:04:49.117 --> 00:04:50.640
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:56.834
A, She is as clever than me.. B, She is as clever as me.. C, She is so clever as me..

82
00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.247
The answer is B: She is as clever as me..

83
00:05:04.383 --> 00:05:06.998
According to the reading, what helps us choose?

84
00:05:07.298 --> 00:05:11.172
A, a comparison. B, a bag. C, a speed.

85
00:05:14.733 --> 00:05:16.814
The answer is A: a comparison.

86
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.570
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:22.417 --> 00:05:25.090
Compare yourself to a friend using 'as...as'.

88
00:05:33.883 --> 00:05:35.244
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:35.544 --> 00:05:47.847
I am as tall as my friend Dara, but I am not as fast as him. He is as friendly as I am. I use as…as for things that are equal and not as…as for things that are different.

90
00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:49.787
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:57.655
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and equality: as plus adjective plus as and not as … as.

92
00:05:57.955 --> 00:06:02.418
Today's value is fairness. Look for solutions that are fair to everyone.

93
00:06:02.718 --> 00:06:05.231
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

94
00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:09.414
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

